{"c":[{"id":"be6d5b2b22a12f2f","sum":"B22: tasks bind to their host connection and are revoked on close, pause, stop or settings change; evals call helper.hostConnected(id). Mutation tests: --build-path /tmp. --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only. Press only whole SAFE_PRESSES labels.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b6ef750a1098cf99","sum":"B22: tasks bind to their host connection, revoked when it closes or on any pause, stop, take over or settings change; executor asks Helper.authorize before each act; evals call helper.hostConnected(id). Return in a field presses the default button, unreported.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"563c0e5f60870996","sum":"Return in a frontmost single-line field presses the default button (5/5), and B21's reader does not report it. B22: each consumer connection is a host session; tasks are revoked when it closes; in-process evals playing the host call helper.hostConnected(id).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T031707Z-b7d2054c5f965771","text":"AppKit presses a window's default button on Return typed into a single-line text field: frontmost fixture, Note focused, Send ran 5 of 5. B21's reader counts no Return while a text field has focus (brief), so that submit goes unreported (gui/keys-front).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150809Z-35454632bb9daf62","text":"B22: each consumer connection is a host session; accepted tasks bind to the one that started them and are revoked when it closes; runs with no Tab need a connected host. In-process tests and evals that play the host must call helper.hostConnected(id) or no skill runs on its own.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"648a97f969b90b5d","sum":"B22: any pause, stop, take over, settings/permission/skill/memory change or host disconnect revokes the act grant; the executor asks Helper.authorize before each write, press, raise and calendar add. Tasks bind to their host session; evals call helper.hostConnected(id).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150824Z-0b7169f06df102c4","text":"B22: every pause, take over, stop, Caret pause, settings/permission/skill/memory change and host disconnect revokes the act grant at once (Executor.revoke/recheck); the executor also asks Helper.authorize right before each write, press, raise and calendar add.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150829Z-581618fb20568b53","text":"B22: each consumer connection is a host session; accepted tasks bind to the session that started them and are revoked when it closes; runs with no Tab need a connected host. In-process tests and evals that play the host must call helper.hostConnected(id).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c52def503bedc2af","sum":"B22: mutation tests use --build-path /tmp and grep 'recorded an issue'; --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only; press only whole SAFE_PRESSES labels, never in system prompts (change both lists + press-risk.json). Rig VM display is 2x pixels.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5df295da363b0505","sum":"B22: run mutation swift tests with --build-path /tmp/... and grep 'recorded an issue' (Swift Testing failures). --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only and caret-fixture pids; window ids are opaque to the helper.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150830Z-a3b40432646c1572","text":"B22: swift test --build-path /tmp/... keeps mutation runs out of .build/debug; Swift Testing marks failures 'recorded an issue', not ✘, so grep that when checking a mutation was caught.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150830Z-cd56cc67608f9643","text":"B22: --act-pids now needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only and caret-fixture pids; window ids are <pid>-<start µs>-<generation>-<n>, opaque to the helper.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6f5c7126a4148883","sum":"B22: presses only whole labels in SAFE_PRESSES/RiskTable.safePresses, never in system prompts; change both lists and press-risk.json together. Rig VM display is pixels at 2x (use 3840x2400 for panels); close fixture forms >=3 s after a routine run.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150843Z-b8f6b3671dd764ee","text":"B22: presses only whole labels in risk.ts SAFE_PRESSES / RiskTable.safePresses, never in a system prompt (subrole AXSystemDialog or AXSystemFloatingWindow, or a TCC/SecurityAgent process); change both lists and press-risk.json together.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T162636Z-ec02bde9a2237805","text":"Rig VM display file is pixels at 2x: 1920x1200 gives a 960x600-pt screen, too small for Caret's panels beside caret-fixture forms; A16's drawn walk uses 3840x2400. Close fixture forms >=3 s after a routine run or the bundle loses a copy and scores a miss.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"91c4298dddb7818a","sum":"Host gotchas: compare field values by UTF-16 or digest, not String ==; the host's hello says host: true; reader marks make undo say notSameElement for a replaced field. caret-screen trusts only a helperAuth-first helper (launch.ts or --auth-fd), in a 0700 socket dir.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"7ff50a1675eceeeb","sum":"T1 and B23 host gotchas: compare field values by UTF-16 or digest, not String ==; spell-check language is a hint only; v2/host must say host: true in its hello; reader marks make undo answer notSameElement for a replaced field.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"60b138f01f887219","sum":"T1: compare field values with .utf16.elementsEqual or digests, never Swift String == (canonical equivalence lets é match e+U+0301); NSSpellChecker's orthography option is only a starting point under automatic language (French passes under en).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T170510Z-7982a134da3a9b97","text":"Swift String == is canonical equivalence (precomposed é equals e+U+0301): guards comparing field values must use .utf16.elementsEqual or digests, or a normalizing app passes a mismatched write (T1 RangeEdit.verify).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T170510Z-ca62d5f751cbf8cc","text":"NSSpellChecker requestChecking treats the orthography option as a starting point: with the system's automatic language on, French text passes under en and tres passes under fr (T1, macOS 26.6).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b105c8e9d793ad2e","sum":"B23: only a consumer hello with host: true is the host (v2/host must send it or no skill runs on its own; evals call helper.hostConnected); forward writes carry a mark, undo sends sameAs, the reader answers notSameElement for any other element (fakes: test/fake-marks.ts).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T171742Z-0e49751b5685c975","text":"B23: only a consumer hello with host: true counts as the host; other consumers bind their own work but keep no run with no Tab alive. v2/host must send host: true, or no skill runs on its own. In-process evals still call helper.hostConnected(id).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T171742Z-101e1e3d273eec2a","text":"B23: forward value writes carry a mark and undo sends sameAs; the reader answers notSameElement unless the element at the key is the one it wrote (per app worker, gone on reader restart). Test fakes use test/fake-marks.ts; marks.replace(windowId, key) plays a replaced field.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"fafcbf0a024798fd","sum":"B23: caret-screen trusts only a helper whose first line is helperAuth (launch via helper/src/launch.ts or --auth-fd); it joins only a 0700 user-owned socket dir (tests use mkdtemp). Crash recovery puts running skills back on Tab; crash-recovery-eval.ts SIGKILLs a real helper.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8a0f27ca66dff765","sum":"B23: crash-recovery-eval.ts SIGKILLs a real helper mid skill run; its 'restarted helper is still running' check catches a crash after the last publish. The reader joins only a 0700 socket dir owned by the user (never /tmp itself): tests use mkdtemp.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T171742Z-362dd90f069eee83","text":"B23: scripts/crash-recovery-eval.ts SIGKILLs a real helper child mid skill run while the script plays reader and host; its 'restarted helper is still running' check is what catches a crash after the last publish (an id collision did exactly that).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T171742Z-7971f1eeb5bd9db9","text":"B23: the reader connects only to a socket whose directory is 0700 and the user's own (never /tmp itself; HelperServer chmods its dir). Tests and evals put sockets in mkdtemp directories.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7bbf7179e42f4b5b","sum":"B23: caret-screen trusts only a helper whose first line is helperAuth (HMAC of challenge+pid); start via helper/src/launch.ts or pass --auth-fd. recovery.sqlite rows of runs under way put their skill back on Tab at start and list as stopped at step N of M with undo.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T171817Z-c0fbce2e0a5b8f78","text":"B23: caret-screen needs --auth-fd (32-byte secret) and trusts only a helper whose first line is helperAuth (HMAC of challenge+pid, pid = LOCAL_PEERPID). Use helper/src/launch.ts; evals pass --auth-fd 0, sendSecret(reader, s), new HelperServer(..., s).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T171834Z-0d54f9ef314f8bad","text":"B23: recovery.sqlite holds sealed rows of runs under way (skill_id in clear). At start each row's skill goes back on Tab; readable rows list as 'Stopped when Caret restarted, at step N of M' with undo. Id generators skip ids in use (idTaken).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
